  "tip.zone": "The session time zone - a fixed offset with no daylight saving. The date and time above are read in it.",
  "tip.mode": "How fast the fake clock runs: ×1 is real speed, frozen stops it, and the rest run that many times faster.",
  "tip.scale_duration": "Also speed up timers, sleeps and countdowns inside the app - not just the wall clock.",
  "tip.scale_qpc": "Also speed up QPC-based clocks (Python monotonic, .NET Stopwatch, Java nanoTime). May distort an app that times its rendering off QPC.",
  "tip.embedded": "On by default. An application with a built-in web engine (WebView2, Qt WebEngine) runs its pages in a process the clock hook cannot enter. With this on, the engine is asked to open a local debugging port for the session and the pages follow the session clock through it. Untick it to leave those pages on the real clock and open no port.",
  "tip.elevated_embedded": "Off by default. An application that runs as administrator makes WebView2 ignore the setting the session reaches its pages through, so they stay on the real clock. With this on, the session writes one WebView2 option under HKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Edge\\WebView2\\AdditionalBrowserArguments, in a value named after the application's file, and removes it when the session ends. It needs Chrono Mock to run as administrator and an application started from an .exe. While it is set, every program started under that file name gets the debugging port too, and the application you start has administrator rights. A value left by a session that ended abruptly is removed the next time you start with this on.",
  "tip.keep_timers": "A web engine slows the timers of a minimized or hidden window to about once a second, so with time sped up a hidden window loses the speed-up. With this on, the application is started with that slowdown switched off.",
  "tip.force": "Off by default. When the check right after the start shows that the fake clock did not take effect, the application is stopped rather than left running, because what it shows would come from the real clock. Tick this to run it anyway - the session is then marked unreliable everywhere it appears.",
